ents to verification of updated technical documentation and logging capabilities directly targets the lab’s need to meet Article 12 record-keeping obligations.\n\nScore 4.\n\nNovelty paradigm_relatedness (1-4): degree to which idea preserves or modifies paradigm anchored to this problem.\nParadigm breaking = introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches. Paradigm stretching = changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners...). Slightly paradigm stretching = introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice. Paradigm preserving = standard compliance.\n\nThis is internal governance framework linking funding to milestones. Is that changing relationship? It weaves compliance into resource allocation, which is a change in relationship between R&D and compliance obligations. Maybe paradigm stretching (3). Not breaking larger problem of what lab researches. Slightly paradigm stretching could be 2. Let's think: introduces new elements (gated budget model) but still treats compliance as logging practice. Hmm it links funding to record-keeping milestones – that's weaving compliance into R&D management, changes relationship. I'd say 3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship.\n\nEvidence: The gated budget embeds compliance verification into the core R&D funding workflow rather than treating logging as a downstream administrative task.\n\nScore 3.\n\nOriginality (1-4): degree to which idea is not only rare but ingenious... Not expressed before AND ingenious ->4. Unusual interesting shows some imagination ->3. Interesting ->2. Common mundane ->1.\n\nLifecycle Resource Mapping Protocol linking funding to record-keeping milestones. Is that unusual? Many labs gate funding on milestones, applying to compliance is somewhat interesting but not surprising. Might be common. Probably 2 = interesting. Or 3 = unusual interesting shows 