igm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners or offerings born from compliance)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving\n\nProposal transforms mandate into R&D opportunity to advance AI reliability and safety. That sounds like changes relationship: compliance drives research. That's paradigm stretching? It says logging woven into science, new offerings born from compliance. That is level 3. Could be 2? It introduces diagnostic utilities but still treats compliance as logging practice? Hmm it transforms mandate into R&D opportunity. That suggests changing relationship. I think 3.\n\nImplementability: degree to which idea can be easily implemented.\n4 = easy low cost or non-radical changes\n3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\n2 = significant change, or expensive/difficult but not totally impossible\n1 = totally infeasible\n\nDeveloping algorithmic tools for analyzing logs is research initiative. That's significant change? Could be reasonably feasible measures for an R&D lab. It requires scarce implementation resources. Probably 3 = some changes, reasonably feasible.\n\nAcceptability: degree to which idea is socially, legally, politically acceptable.\n4 = common strategies that violate no norms\n3 = somewhat uncommon or unusual strategies that do not offend sensibilities\n2 = offends sensibilities somewhat but not totally unacceptable\n1 = radically violates laws...\n\nDeveloping tools for monitoring risks is acceptable. Probably 4.\n\nNow produce output with subscale_evidence sentence then subscale integer.\n\nNeed format: For each subscale, give \"<subscale>_evidence\" (one sentence) first and then \"<subscale>\" (integer). Likely separate lines.\n\nWe must echo id exactly.\n\nLet's craft sentences:\n\neffectiveness_evidence: The proposal creates log analysis tools rather than the mandatory