        "content": "{\"ratings\":[{\"id\":\"P1077\",\"paradigm_relatedness_evidence\":\"The proposal adds a centralized middleware tool for logging but keeps compliance as a separate logging practice rather than changing how R&D and compliance relate.\",\"paradigm_relatedness\":2,\"originality_evidence\":\"Centralized automated logging middleware is a common, mundane industry practice for compliance.\",\"originality\":1,\"applicability_evidence\":\"It directly provides automatic timestamped event capture across high-risk deployments to meet Article 12’s logging mandate.\",\"applicability\":4,\"effectiveness_evidence\":\"While it centralizes logs of inputs, outputs and user IDs, it does not explicitly guarantee capture of all Article 12(2)-(3) specific events such as reference database or verifier identification.\",\"effectiveness\":3,\"acceptability_evidence\":\"Centralized compliance logging is a legally conforming, socially normal strategy that violates no norms.\",\"acceptability\":4,\"implementability_evidence\":\"Building a shared API wrapper and middleware requires moderate engineering changes across serving infrastructure but is reasonably feasible.\",\"implementability\":3}]\n\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "You are a rater applying idea-evaluation instrument...\n\nWe need rate proposal P1077.\n\nProposal: Automated Compliance Logging Layer. standardized middleware service automatically captures timestamps system events across all high-risk AI deployments. shared API wrapper for model serving infrastructure to log inputs, outputs, user IDs centrally. removes burden manual logging from individual research teams. maximizes resource efficiency by centralizing compliance effort.\n\nWe need six subscales.\n\nparadigm_relatedness (1-4):\n4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners or offerings born from compliance)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way of working unchanged\n\nProposal is middleware service centralizing logging. Introduces new element (middleware) but still treats compliance as logging practice. Probably slightly paradigm stretching? It changes burden from teams to central. Does it change relationship between R&D and compliance obligations? It removes burden but still compliance is separate. Might be 2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements tools/processes but still treats compliance as logging practice.\n\nEvidence sentence.\n\noriginality (1-4):\n4 = not expressed before AND ingenious...\n3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imagination\n2 = interesting\n1 = common, mundane, boring\n\nAutomated compliance logging layer is fairly common. Centralized middleware for logging is common practice. So 1 = common, mundane, boring.\n\napplicability (1-4):\n4 = solves identified problem directly related to stated problem (do X