rly applies to stated problem. Solves identified problem directly related? Do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem. Yes, ensure logs contain mandatory fields required by Article 12. That's directly related to meeting logging mandate. So applicability 4 = solves an identified problem that is directly related.\n\nWorkability implementability: degree can be easily implemented. Build script parses log files against checklist. Seems easy to implement at low cost, non-radical changes. So implementability 4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes.\n\nAcceptability: degree socially legally politically acceptable. Common strategies that violate no norms. Checking compliance internally is common. So acceptability 4 = common strategies that violate no norms.\n\nNovelty paradigm_relatedness: degree to which idea preserves/modifies paradigm anchored to this problem.\n4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners or offerings born from compliance)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way of working unchanged\n\nProposal is a verification tool, pre-deployment gatekeeper. Introduces new tool but still treats compliance as logging practice. Probably slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools) but still treats compliance as logging practice. So paradigm_relatedness = 2.\n\nOriginality: degree to which idea is not only rare but also ingenious... 4 = not expressed before AND ingenious... 3 = unusual interesting shows some imagination 2 = interesting 1 = common mundane boring\n\nAutomated compliance auditor script checking logs against checklist is fairly