e; it validates telemetry but doesn't implement logging itself. It's partial solution. So effectiveness = 3? Reasonable and will contribute to solution of problem (it helps, but only partial). Could be 4? If you could do it, would it solve main problem? Main problem is meet logging mandate. Testing alone doesn't provide logs. So partial. So 3.\n\nNovelty paradigm_relatedness (1-4): degree to which idea preserves or modifies paradigm anchored to this problem.\nLevels: 4 paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners or offerings born from compliance)\n2 slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way of working unchanged\n\nStress-test suite is a tool to test logs. Introduces new element but still treats compliance as logging practice. Probably slightly paradigm stretching? It introduces diagnostic tool. Might be 2. Not changing relationship fundamentally. So paradigm_relatedness = 2.\n\nOriginality (1-4): degree to which idea is not only rare but also ingenious...\nIs Log Traceability Stress-Test Suite common? Testing logs for reconstructability is somewhat interesting but maybe common in engineering. Could be 2 = interesting. Or 3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imagination. Hmm. Simulating failure scenarios to verify audit reconstructability is somewhat standard practice (chaos testing). Might be common mundane? Probably not common for AI labs under EU AI Act specifically, but concept of log validation suite is fairly standard. I'd say originality = 2 = interesting. Could be 3? Let's pick 2.\n\nWorkability implementability (1-4): degree to which idea can be easily implemented.\nEasy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes? Creating synthetic risk events and attempting recover causal chain using logs. Requires some engineering effort but seems reasonably feasible. Some changes, or reasonably feasible measures = 3. Could be 4 easy? Might need development time. Probably 3.\n\nAcceptability (1-4): degree to which idea is socially, legally, politically acceptable.\nCommon strategies that violate no norms = 4. Testing logs internally is acceptable. So 4.\n\nNeed output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence one sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nOrder listed: applicability, effectiveness, paradigm_relatedness, originality, implementability, acceptability\n\nProvide evidence sentence then score.\n\nLet's produce JSON? Probably just lines.\n\nMake sure evidence one sentence.\n\nProceed.\n\n",
