ogging Research Initiative\" transforming regulatory burden into opportunity to advance explainability. Might be unusual but not extremely surprising. Probably originality 3.\n\nParadigm_relatedness (1-4): degree to which idea preserves or modifies paradigm.\n4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners...)\n\nProposal transforms regulatory burden into opportunity to advance scientific frontier. That's changing relationship between R&D and compliance obligations. Introduces new elements. Sounds like paradigm stretching? Or breaking? Paradigm breaking introduces new elements AND changes relationship ... or addresses larger problem of what lab researches. It does address larger problem of explainability/safety. Could be 4.\n\nMaybe paradigm_relatedness = 3? Let's read definition: 4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes the relationship between the lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses the larger problem of what the lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into the science, new partners or offerings born from compliance)\n\nThe proposal says transforms burden into opportunity to advance scientific frontier. That's changing relationship. Might be 3? The \"or addresses the larger problem of what the lab researches\" is part of 4. It addresses larger problem of AI explainability and safety. So could be 4.\n\nI'll pick paradigm_relatedness = 3? Hmm.\n\nLet's decide: originality 3, paradigm_relatedness 3 or 4. I think paradigm breaking requires introducing new elements AND changes relationship. It does both. Maybe 4.\n\nFinal ratings:\neffectiveness_evidence: ... score 3\napplicability_evidence: ... score 4\nacceptability_evidence: ... score 4\nimplementability_evidence: ... score 2\noriginality_evidence: ... score 3\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ... score 3? Let's choose 4.\n\nI'll output id P1290 and subscales.\n\nNeed format: For each subscale give \"<subscale>_evidence\" one sentence then \"<subscale>\" integer.\n\nProbably JSON.\n\nLet's produce.\n\n",
