ble.\nCommon strategies that violate no norms =4. This is acceptable. Score 4.\n\nEvidence: Offloading technical logging work to specialists is socially and legally unobjectionable in regulated R&D settings.\n\nimplementability (1-4): degree to which idea can be easily implemented.\nEasy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes =4. Hiring two engineers and reallocating budget is reasonably feasible. Might be some changes =>3? \"reallocate a small percentage of operational budget to hire two dedicated compliance engineers\". That's some changes, reasonably feasible. Could be 3.\n\nAnchored: 4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\n3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\n\nHiring two people is some change. Probably 3.\n\nEvidence: Hiring two engineers requires budget reallocation and recruitment but does not demand fundamental technology redesign.\n\nLet's output format.\n\nNeed echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>.\n\nProbably JSON? The instruction says return rating... For each subscale give ... first and then... Probably output lines.\n\nWe'll produce:\n\nid: P1936\neffectiveness_evidence: ...\neffectiveness: 4\netc.\n\nEnsure order listed: effectiveness, applicability, paradigm_relatedness, originality, acceptability, implementability\n\nLet's craft sentences one sentence each.\n\nProceed.",
