lity 4, implementability 2.\n\nNeed format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence one sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProvide output.\n\nProbably JSON? Instruction says return rating... Provide maybe list.\n\nI'll output lines:\n\nid: P2450\noriginality_evidence: ...\noriginality:3\netc.\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's craft concise sentences.\n\noriginality_evidence: The proposal combines automated log-to-model provenance with an immutable ledger to repurpose compliance data for research, which is unusual and shows imagination beyond standard logging.\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: It weaves regulatory logging into scientific practice by turning logs into a causal-behavior dataset, changing how R&D and compliance relate.\n\neffectiveness_evidence: If implemented, the API-driven provenance chain would automatically record required events and metadata, directly satisfying Article 12 traceability.\n\napplicability_evidence: The framework is explicitly designed to meet the high-risk logging mandate and adapt R&D workflows accordingly.\n\nacceptability_evidence: Centralized immutable logging of system telemetry for compliance is legally aligned with the AI Act and does not offend norms.\n\nimplementability_evidence: Deploying a standardized API layer across all high-risk projects and an immutable ledger requires significant engineering effort and cost.\n\nReturn.",
